.TH VDR-SUITE-HUMAN-ACCOUNT-RECOVER 8 "September 2026" "VDR-Suite" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
vdr-suite-human-account-recover \- locally rotate one existing Human Account password credential
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vdr-suite-human-account-recover
.BI --account-id " ID"
.BI --login " LOGIN"
.RI [ --database " PATH" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vdr-suite-human-account-recover
is a local root-only administration command for audited Human Account recovery.
It rotates the selected existing Human Account's normal
.B human-password
credential inside the existing Suite security authority.
.PP
The command does not create a second Human Account, Actor, administrator grant
or recovery store. It does not reveal the existing password or stored verifier.
The account identifier and login name must select the same active Human Account
and active
.B human-password
credential.
.PP
Recovery creates one replacement
.B human-password
credential for the same Actor, records the replaced credential as its rotation
predecessor, moves the login verifier to the replacement and revokes the
predecessor. This fences a stale password-authenticated request that has not yet
reached browser-session issuance.
.PP
The new password is converted to a yescrypt verifier. The command does not
accept the new password as a command-line argument. On an interactive terminal
it prompts twice with terminal echo disabled. With redirected standard input it
reads exactly one password line.
.PP
All still-active browser sessions issued from the replaced human-password
credential are revoked in the same SQLite transaction as credential rotation,
verifier replacement and successful accountability evidence. The Human Account
identifier, Actor identifier and existing permission grants are left unchanged.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --account-id " ID"
Select the explicit existing Human Account to recover.
.TP
.BI --login " LOGIN"
Select the existing login credential that must belong to that Human Account and
have credential type
.BR human-password .
.TP
.BI --database " PATH"
Use the specified Suite database instead of
.IR /var/lib/vdr-suite/vdr-suite.db .
.SH OUTPUT
On success the command prints only non-secret identifiers and the number of
revoked browser sessions:
.PP
.nf
account_id=...
replaced_credential_id=...
credential_id=...
revoked_browser_sessions=...
.fi
.SH SECURITY
The command must be run as root. There is no remote anonymous recovery endpoint
and no Public-v1 recovery mutation. Password plaintext and stored verifiers are
not persisted outside their existing one-way verifier authority and are not
included in accountability events.
.PP
Expected semantic failures such as an unknown, inactive or mismatched account or
credential are recorded as denied recovery evidence without password material.
The audit actor identifies the local recovery system authority rather than the
target Human Account. A persistence or accountability failure prevents the
credential, verifier and session mutation from committing.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/vdr-suite/vdr-suite.db
Default Suite security database.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vdr-suite-daemon (8),
.BR vdr-suite-first-admin-bootstrap (8)
